Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.61,0:00:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU, YAMU!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.47,0:00:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You're on the move!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.81,0:01:08.05,Default,,0,0,0,,You're teetering on the edge\Nof the Shadow Realm, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.89,0:01:12.09,Default,,0,0,0,,One false move and you'll\Nbe trapped for eternity.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.55,0:01:18.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, well if I were you, I\Nwouldn't get my hopes up, Akura.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.15,0:01:19.19,Default,,0,0,0,,And why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.61,0:01:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to the special effect\Nof my cursed twin dolls,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.27,0:01:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,every card that was sent to my former\Ngraveyard was just released onto the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.11,0:01:30.11,Default,,0,0,0,,But you, on the other hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.63,0:01:33.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, let's just say\Nyou've seen better duels.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.95,0:01:37.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Too bad you can't bring out\Nthe Pharaoh to save you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.23,0:01:39.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe not, but I can save him!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.63,0:01:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Just as soon as I beat Bakura\Nand get out of this place!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.31,0:01:48.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Now that my twins are\Nfinished, why don't you go? Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.25,0:01:49.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I was hoping you'd say that!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.29,0:01:51.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Not so fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.21,0:01:56.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm afraid you just triggered the\Nspecial effect of my necro-soldier.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.47,0:02:00.79,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as he remains on the\Nfield, every time your turn begins,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.17,0:02:03.49,Default,,0,0,0,,my necro army increases by one.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.27,0:02:08.83,Default,,0,0,0,,And since this ability applies\Nto my new soldier as well,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.11,0:02:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I now have an army of three.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.53,0:02:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,As you were.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.05,0:02:17.58,Default,,0,0,0,,How's Yugi supposed to beat an\Narmy of little zombie freaks?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.19,0:02:22.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Actually, since each of his soldiers has\Nzero points, it shouldn't be too tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.65,0:02:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Here goes!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.93,0:02:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,First, my Silent Swordsman jumps\Nto level 5 with 3500 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.33,0:02:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's just the beginning!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.23,0:02:35.05,Default,,0,0,0,,To accompany my Silent Swordsman,\NI'll summon my Silent Magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.43,0:02:40.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, Marshmellon,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.29,0:02:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Silent Swordsman and Silent Magician\Nattack all three of his Necro-soldiers!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.59,0:02:46.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.61,0:02:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Once Vakura's troop of\NNecro-corps is gone, Yugi wins!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.81,0:03:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.05,0:03:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But why did my swordsman stop?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.87,0:03:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't make any sense!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.65,0:03:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Of course it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.97,0:03:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I've played my Narrow Corridor Trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.25,0:03:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and what does that do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.21,0:03:16.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad you asked, Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.47,0:03:18.81,Default,,0,0,0,,This handy track card\Nprevents your friends from
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.89,0:03:21.63,Default,,0,0,0,,attacking with more than two\Nmonsters in any given turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.71,0:03:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And might I remind you,\Nmy graveyard's gone,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.17,0:03:29.41,Default,,0,0,0,,so the soldiers you just destroyed\Nshall return to the field as spirits.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.61,0:03:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you don't mind if my phantom\Nmonsters stick around to watch me win.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.29,0:03:41.39,Default,,0,0,0,,What I want to know is, what's he\Nplanning to do with all those monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.47,0:03:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take over from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.97,0:03:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, did I mention my\Nmagician's special ability?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.99,0:03:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,When you draw, he jumps up one\Nlevel and gains 500 points!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.51,0:03:54.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Should I be impressed?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.81,0:03:59.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, just the card I was hoping to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.95,0:04:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The time has come to\Nreveal my true strategy.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.17,0:04:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,True strategy?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.09,0:04:08.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, is that an echo in here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.69,0:04:11.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold my counterbalance magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.29,0:04:13.73,Default,,0,0,0,,What does that do?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.13,0:04:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as this card remains on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.35,0:04:20.45,Default,,0,0,0,,each of us must transfer a\Ncertain number of cards from
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.53,0:04:25.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Our deck to our graveyard at\Nthe end of our turn. How many
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.11,0:04:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,you ask you must discard as\Nmany cards as there are monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.75,0:04:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,on the field of course that\Nincludes my phantom monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.73,0:04:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,no way then we'd be throwing\Nout practically our entire deck
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.63,0:04:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,but why would you play a card\Nthat puts you at risk also.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.45,0:04:45.98,Default,,0,0,0,,It doesn't make any sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.99,0:04:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,To work, it requires a graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.75,0:04:52.53,Default,,0,0,0,,And I don't have one.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.85,0:04:55.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess that means I can't participate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.57,0:04:56.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel so left out.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.17,0:04:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So you're in this alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.33,0:05:00.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Get it?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.55,0:05:03.01,Default,,0,0,0,,This card only drains your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.79,0:05:05.99,Default,,0,0,0,,So that was your plan all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.23,0:05:08.94,Default,,0,0,0,,You wanted to force me\Nto get rid of my cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.81,0:05:10.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.11,0:05:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuki's only got a few turns left. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.49,0:05:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And it only gets worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.39,0:05:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,For now, I summon another\Nmonster to the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.35,0:05:21.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Necro Mannequin!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.25,0:05:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's not all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.07,0:05:27.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, I activate the trap card.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.17,0:05:29.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Necro Cycle!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.75,0:05:32.49,Default,,0,0,0,,As long as my mannequin\Nremains on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.71,0:05:36.59,Default,,0,0,0,,this trap allows me to automatically\Nsummon another one each turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.61,0:05:39.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at all those monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.33,0:05:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,And just think, every one of them\Nrepresents a card you're going to lose!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.39,0:05:53.35,Default,,0,0,0,,And all the fun begins in your next move,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.65,0:05:56.95,Default,,0,0,0,,so I see no need to drag\Nthe suspense out any longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.33,0:05:59.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I end my turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.81,0:06:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Stand back, I shall handle this
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.33,0:06:14.45,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Sork is mine, my king.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.81,0:06:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't. It's the only way.\NWe've tried everything in our power.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.97,0:06:25.07,Default,,0,0,0,,But nothing works. There's one hope\Nleft, and it lies in my hand, Sork.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.47,0:06:28.07,Default,,0,0,0,,you've invaded my kingdom\NAnd threatened my people
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.15,0:06:32.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And now you must pay for\Nyour crime Millennium puzzle,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.35,0:06:33.19,Default,,0,0,0,,activate
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.13,0:06:44.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I shall call upon\Nthe three Egyptian gods!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.91,0:06:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk the Tormentor, Slifer the Sky\NDragon, and the Winged Dragon of Ra!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.73,0:07:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Your fate is now sealed!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.05,0:07:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Behold, the gods of Egypt!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.45,0:07:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, it appears the game\Nhas shifted in my favor.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.15,0:07:28.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Your creatures are no match for Zok.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.71,0:07:31.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I should know since he and\NI are one and the same!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.21,0:07:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.12,0:07:36.77,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean, you are Zork?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.53,0:07:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Surprise?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.44,0:07:41.93,Default,,0,0,0,,How's that for a twist?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.29,0:07:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, let's go in for a\Ncloser look, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.49,0:08:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Surrender now, Zork!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.19,0:08:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Or face the rage of the\Nthree Egyptian gods!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.49,0:08:14.43,Default,,0,0,0,,When I am through with them, your deities\Nshall bow before the Lord of Darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.39,0:08:21.19,Default,,0,0,0,,No way! It's them!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.27,0:08:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Slifer, Obelisk, and Ra!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.75,0:08:26.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But they seem way too\Nrealistic to be holograms.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.95,0:08:28.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Can they be the real deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.71,0:08:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Obelisk!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.62,0:08:32.02,Default,,0,0,0,,The first attack is yours!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.29,0:08:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Strike him down with your fist of fate!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.91,0:08:47.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.33,0:08:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a bad start, but let's\Nsee if Yugi can keep this up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.95,0:08:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Lightning for the Sky Dragon!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.95,0:09:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Lay down your judgment\Nupon this enemy of Egypt!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.35,0:09:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, Winged Dragon of Roar!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.67,0:09:13.20,Default,,0,0,0,,May your eternal light\Nbanish the darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.81,0:09:30.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, my friends, combine\Nyour strength and end this!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.97,0:09:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Fist of Fury, Thunder Force\NAttack, and Blaze Cannon Blast!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.71,0:09:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Finish him off!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.69,0:10:15.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It's over.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.95,0:10:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We're saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.43,0:10:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's hope so.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.95,0:10:31.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, the darkness has lifted.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.61,0:10:34.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, Zork is gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.87,0:10:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,All hail the Egyptian gods. We're free.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.03,0:10:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You did it, Pharaoh. We did.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.19,0:10:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Zork.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.15,0:10:46.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.69,0:10:47.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Can it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.19,0:10:54.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do it! Our sun!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.05,0:10:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.69,0:11:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He's covering Egypt in complete darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.51,0:11:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Somehow that thing just\Ncaused a solar eclipse.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:12.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Egyptian gods, attack\Nbefore the light is gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.27,0:11:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, hurry!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.79,0:11:28.13,Default,,0,0,0,,As the darkness spreads,\Nmy strength grows!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.57,0:11:31.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Die!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.57,0:11:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It's almost gone!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.39,0:11:39.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Raw and sliver, attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.25,0:11:51.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Without the sun's rays, you\Nare powerless against me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.59,0:11:55.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Now prepare to be\Nconsumed by the darkness!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.45,0:12:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The Egyptian gods! He beat them! But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.11,0:12:19.15,Default,,0,0,0,,This can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.23,0:12:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,That was our last hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.67,0:12:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We lost. That's nuts.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.07,0:12:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,No one defeats those monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.45,0:12:30.55,Default,,0,0,0,,There is nothing left to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.77,0:12:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now all hope is lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.63,0:12:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Egyptian gods are shadows\Nof their former selves.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.75,0:12:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Let them crumble along with your hope.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.35,0:12:48.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Carol, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.13,0:12:51.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.27,0:12:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,You lose a card for every monster on the\Nfield, and so far there are ten. Oh yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.89,0:13:04.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Not for long First, my silent swordsman\Nincreases one level and 500 points Hold on,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.01,0:13:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Your monsters aren't the only ones\Nwho can do tricks, Necro-mannequin.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.91,0:13:11.57,Default,,0,0,0,,show Yugi your newest talent
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.27,0:13:16.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Now there's a total of\N11 monsters on the field
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.13,0:13:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,How's Yugi supposed to get\Nrid of all those monsters?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.27,0:13:24.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, didn't Bakura play some card\Nthat limits Yugi's attacks or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.85,0:13:25.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Right you are.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.97,0:13:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Narrow Corridor, to be exact.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.03,0:13:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,And it limits Yugi to two\Nattacks per turn. Plus,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.53,0:13:33.09,Default,,0,0,0,,thanks to my Necro Twins,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.25,0:13:37.19,Default,,0,0,0,,whatever monsters he destroys will\Nreturn to the field as phantoms.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.63,0:13:38.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.05,0:13:43.53,Default,,0,0,0,,First, my swordsman will attack your\NNecro Soldier with Silent Sword Slash.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.61,0:13:48.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And then I'm sending my Silent Magician\Nto destroy your Necro Mannequin! Now go!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.95,0:13:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad, but your turn is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.89,0:13:57.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And you know what that means.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.35,0:14:00.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Eleven cards go to your graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.19,0:14:05.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, if my math is correct, that\Nleaves seventeen cards in your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.19,0:14:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And once they're all gone, game over.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.79,0:14:10.62,Default,,0,0,0,,However,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.70,0:14:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,my twins will make sure\Nyour turn doesn't end on
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.03,0:14:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,a sour note by giving you\N1,200 extra life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.69,0:14:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Sounds good to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.15,0:14:20.19,Default,,0,0,0,,And why are you so chipper?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.51,0:14:23.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, for one, my magician\Njust got stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.17,0:14:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's going to take much more\Nthan that to save you now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.89,0:14:30.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I just summoned my Necro Wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.63,0:14:33.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This lets me increase my\Nmonster army by adding Necro
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.79,0:14:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Wall tokens equal to the\Nnumber of zombies on the field,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.97,0:14:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Which gives me two extra monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.69,0:14:41.15,Default,,0,0,0,,He cared. He did.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.57,0:14:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now say hello to the two newest additions\Nto my ever-growing collection of monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.57,0:14:47.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Necro Wall Token No.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.85,0:14:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,1 and Necro Wall Token No. 2.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.53,0:14:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,That gives me a grand total of 14.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.43,0:14:54.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Now make your final move.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.33,0:14:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,This duel's not over yet, Makura.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.71,0:14:59.77,Default,,0,0,0,,First, my Swordsman gets a boost.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.05,0:15:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Now get ready for another double attack.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.41,0:15:04.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Silent Swordsman attack\Nis wall token number
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.95,0:15:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,one and Silent Magician\Nattack token number two!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.67,0:15:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Very impressive, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.85,0:15:20.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, since you've used up your\Ntwo attack limit, your turn is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.67,0:15:25.81,Default,,0,0,0,,That may be true, but I can still\Nactivate my aria from beyond magic card!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.03,0:15:28.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It allows me to choose\Nany magic card that has
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.49,0:15:31.69,Default,,0,0,0,,already been removed from\Nthe game and reactivate it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.53,0:15:34.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And I choose one of yours!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.37,0:15:35.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Spirit Sword of Sailing!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.63,0:15:40.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm using it to imprison\None of my own monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.17,0:15:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,My Silent Swordsman!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.03,0:15:50.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it me, or did he just\Nharpoon his best card?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.01,0:15:52.03,Default,,0,0,0,,That's so weird!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.25,0:15:55.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Bacora has a field full of\Nmonsters, and Yuki targets his own?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.89,0:15:57.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That ends my turn!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.45,0:15:59.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Glad to hear it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.39,0:16:01.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then, discard 11 cards.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.93,0:16:07.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You may gain a few life points,\Nbut you lose most of your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.25,0:16:16.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Just one more turn, and all\Nof your cards will be gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.65,0:16:20.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And victory will be mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.11,0:16:27.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You know, I probably could\Nend my turn right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.45,0:16:30.41,Default,,0,0,0,,forcing you to discard the\Nrest of your deck immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.49,0:16:33.73,Default,,0,0,0,,But I think watching you\Nsquirm would be much more fun.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.01,0:16:37.63,Default,,0,0,0,,So instead, I'll summon my\NNecro-Jar in attack mode.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.41,0:16:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Now attack his silent magician!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.43,0:16:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,But why?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.79,0:16:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, doesn't Yuki's monster have\Nmore attack points than Vakora's?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.25,0:16:53.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You just gave up almost\Nall of your life points!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.61,0:16:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Why would you do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.57,0:16:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.45,0:16:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,It was all a part of my master plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.13,0:17:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, thanks to my Necrochar,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.51,0:17:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,you must discard one card for\Nevery 300 points I just lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.39,0:17:12.25,Default,,0,0,0,,And since my damage was 1,400, you\Nlose four cards from your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.31,0:17:15.65,Default,,0,0,0,,So off to the graveyard they go.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.07,0:17:17.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a second.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.59,0:17:20.49,Default,,0,0,0,,That's gonna leave Yugi\Nwith only one card left.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.05,0:17:26.09,Default,,0,0,0,,And so the end is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.17,0:17:30.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Not only the end of our duel, but\Nthe end of the world as we know it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.71,0:17:34.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Why, with you trapped in the Shadow\NRealm, the pharaoh will never defeat Sork.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.07,0:17:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Now let's review, shall we?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.45,0:17:43.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Twelve monsters remain on the field, and\Nyou have only one card left in your deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.67,0:17:47.39,Default,,0,0,0,,And as we all know, when you\Nrun out of cards, you lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.51,0:17:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I knew it all along.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.63,0:17:52.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Without the pharaoh, you're nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.75,0:17:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,He's the king of games.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.57,0:17:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just a frightened child.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.25,0:18:02.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, don't listen to\Na word this creep says.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.29,0:18:03.23,Default,,0,0,0,,You can do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.57,0:18:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Tay is right, pal.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.83,0:18:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,He's just trying to psych you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.71,0:18:07.54,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.03,0:18:10.47,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm the only one being honest with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.87,0:18:13.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Think about every important\Nduel you've ever fought.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.09,0:18:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Who was doing all the work?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.05,0:18:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The Pharaoh, that's who.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.51,0:18:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe he's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.87,0:18:33.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi, I can't do this without you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.79,0:18:35.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, help me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.85,0:18:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The future of mankind depends on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.01,0:18:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,The barrow needs me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.99,0:18:45.21,Default,,0,0,0,,And this duel's still on.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.43,0:18:48.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I have one cart left\Nand that's all I need.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.49,0:18:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.11,0:18:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now win.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.81,0:18:54.15,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you expect to do with one card?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.99,0:19:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrificed my marshmallow and my\Nsilent magician so I can summon this!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.77,0:19:03.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Gandorra, the Dragon of Destruction!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.51,0:19:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Not that!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.63,0:19:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Makura,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:11.63,0:19:14.59,Default,,0,0,0,,the game's not over till\Nthe last card is played and
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.67,0:19:18.89,Default,,0,0,0,,my last card is the one with\Nthe power to stop you! But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.09,0:19:20.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I have a field full of monsters!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.95,0:19:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,and you only have one!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.39,0:19:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Gandora, activate your special ability!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.63,0:19:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Boundless Giga Rays!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.97,0:19:38.89,Default,,0,0,0,,No!
